# `entire review` Spawn-Time Agent Picker — Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-22-entire-review-spawn-agent-picker-design.md`

**Goal:** When `entire review` is run with more than one eligible (configured + hooks-installed) agent and no `--agent` flag, prompt the user to pick which agent runs instead of silently defaulting to alphabetical-first.

**Architecture:** Small addition to `cmd/entire/cli/review.go`: a `promptForAgent` helper using `NewAccessibleForm(huh.NewSelect[string]())`, a tiny `runReviewDeps` struct with a `promptForAgentFn` injection hook for testing, and a pre-check in `runReview` that computes the three-way `eligibleConfigured` set and invokes the picker only when len > 1 and no override is set. `selectReviewAgent` is unchanged.

