```

**Test 2: Orchestrator-level ctx-cancel kills long-running fake agent quickly**

In `cmd/entire/cli/review_multi_test.go`:

```go
// TestOrchestrator_CtxCancelTerminatesWithinBudget pins that cancelling
// the parent context kills a long-running subprocess within a small
// budget (not the 5s watchdog — the default ctx-cancel path via
// exec.CommandContext's SIGKILL). This is the regression guard for the
// Ctrl+C cancel path: even though the TUI captures KeyCtrlC rather than
// SIGINT, the orchestrator-level cancel via cancelRun() still works.
func TestOrchestrator_CtxCancelTerminatesWithinBudget(t *testing.T) {
    // Cannot t.Parallel — uses global marker.
    env := setupReviewTestRepoWithCommit(t)

    // Fake agent that would run for 10 seconds if not killed.
    tasks := []MultiAgentTask{
        {Name: "long", Prompt: "x", Agent: &fakeHeadlessAgent{name: "long", output: "", delay: 10 * time.Second}},
    }

    ctx, cancel := context.WithCancel(context.Background())
    orch := newMultiReviewOrchestrator(env) // or whatever the existing signature is

    // Cancel after the subprocess has had a chance to start.
    go func() {
        time.Sleep(100 * time.Millisecond)
        cancel()
    }()

    start := time.Now()
    result, _ := orch.Run(ctx, tasks, io.Discard)
    elapsed := time.Since(start)

    // 2s budget: subprocess should die well before its 10s delay expires.
    // WaitDelay=500ms + process teardown ~100ms + scheduling slack = ~2s.
    if elapsed > 2*time.Second {
        t.Errorf("ctx cancel didn't kill subprocess fast enough: %v (want ≤2s)", elapsed)
    }

    // The run was cancelled (not "done").
    if len(result.Runs) > 0 && result.Runs[0].Status == AgentRunDone {
        t.Errorf("expected cancelled/failed, got Done")
    }
}
```

If an existing `TestOrchestrator_CancelCleansMarker` or similar test exists that already covers this budget check, SKIP duplicating — note it in your report.

